[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Authored comprehensive unit tests for the DAG engine singletons: node add/edge/remove semantics, deferred dependency validation, duplicate/nonexistent node precondition errors, acyclicity and CycleError detection, deterministic topological sort with priority/lexicographic tie-breaking, roots/leaves, weighted critical path, wave scheduler state transitions and all three failure policies, is_finished terminal/blocked/empty cases, and DAGRunner happy-path execution, retries, failure recording, and FAIL_FAST/SKIP_DOWNSTREAM/CONTINUE_ON_ERROR behavior. Verified with bin/check_files.
[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite.py: Implemented the library interface: concrete exception dataclasses (non-frozen DAGError/CycleError/NodeNotFoundError/DuplicateNodeError/NodeExecutionError with __str__ delegating to message so Python can assign __traceback__), frozen data types (NodeDefinition, NodeResult, DAGRunReport), NodeState/FailurePolicy enums, and @singleton_type service protocols (DAG, WaveScheduler, DAGRunner) with contract docstrings mirroring low/dag_engine_lite.pyi.
[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Implemented the concrete DAG engine: (1) DAG with _nodes/_upstream/_downstream adjacency, DuplicateNodeError on duplicate add_node, deferred dependency existence checks (NodeNotFoundError raised from validate/topological_sort), add_edge/remove_node with incident edge purging, deterministic priority-desc/id-asc Kahn topological sort, DFS cycle detection raising CycleError with the cycle sequence, find_roots/find_leaves, and longest-path dynamic programming with backtracking for compute_critical_path; (2) WaveScheduler syncing _states from the registered DAG (purging removed nodes, initializing roots READY / blocked nodes PENDING), priority-ordered next_wave, mark_running/mark_succeeded promotion of unblocked dependents, mark_failed realizing FAIL_FAST (cancel remaining non-terminal), SKIP_DOWNSTREAM (skip transitive dependents), and CONTINUE_ON_ERROR (skip only ancestors blocked by failures), plus is_finished/get_state/get_all_states with NodeNotFoundError precondition; (3) DAGRunner.run validating the graph, executing sequential waves with per-node retries, reifying action exceptions into NodeResult records, applying failure policies, halting on FAIL_FAST, and returning a consolidated DAGRunReport with wall-clock timing, critical path and sorted outcome tuples. The CLEANROOM AUTO-GENERATED __initialize__ block was left untouched.
