[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Resolved all four [from:coverage] unreachable-logic facets by annotating each assumed-unreachable internal-invariant guard with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: <witness>)' per the companion guide (guides/low_to_lib.md), quoting the exact witness assumption instead of pruning the defensive checks: (1) topological_sort dangling downstream-adjacency guard -> assumption: adjacency_invariants (every downstream member is a registered node, so the indegree guard cannot fire); (2) validate/DFS cycle-scan unregistered-dependent guard -> assumption: registered_downstream_members (dependents are always registered nodes); (3) WaveScheduler._has_blocking_ancestor unregistered dependency-state guard -> assumption: dependencies_validated_before_scheduling (every dependency is a registered, synced node); (4) DAGRunner.run empty-wave halt guard -> assumption: validated_graph_no_stalled_waves (a validated graph always yields a progressing ready wave until all nodes are terminal). The guard branches are retained (not pruned) because they enforce internal consistency invariants and the halt guard is the loop-safety terminator; each is now excluded from coverage via the documented pragma form so no dead logic is measured. No behavioral changes; static checks pass and all other logic is unchanged.
