[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/dag_engine_lite/tests/dag_engine_lite_impl_test.py: Resolved the remaining continue_on_error coverage feedback: added test_mark_failed_continue_on_error_leaves_independent_branch_ancestors_untouched. The test builds a failed branch (a -> b -> c) alongside an independent multi-level branch (x -> x2 -> y) whose ancestors are non-terminal, marks a FAILED under CONTINUE_ON_ERROR, asserts only b and c become SKIPPED while x stays READY and x2/y stay PENDING, then drives the independent branch to completion and asserts is_finished transitions correctly. This covers independent branch traversal with the failed node outside the branch and non-terminal ancestor states. Verified with bin/check_files.
[CHANGE] benchmark_4/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Pruned the dead cyclic-graph fallback path instead of annotating it. (1) topological_sort (formerly lines 167-168, topology='cycle_tuple_fallback'): a Kahn ordering shortfall necessarily implies a directed cycle, so the 'if cycle is None: cycle = tuple(sorted(n for n in self._nodes if indegree.get(n, 0) > 0))' fallback was unreachable dead logic and is now removed; topological_sort raises CycleError directly from the cycle sequence resolved by _find_cycle(). (2) Restructured _find_cycle to return Tuple[str, ...] using an empty tuple as the acyclic sentinel rather than Optional[None], so validate() now performs a single 'if cycle:' check whose acyclic and cyclic outcomes are both reachable and no dead narrowing branch remains (empty tuple is falsy; a detected cycle is always non-empty since it repeats the closing node). (3) Audited sibling branches for the same unreachable-fallback pattern and pruned the equivalent dead fallback in compute_critical_path ('leaf_nodes if leaf_nodes else order'): a non-empty acyclic graph always has at least one leaf, so the fallback to the full ordering could never execute; terminal-node selection now operates directly over the leaf candidate list. All reachable behavior is unchanged (cycle detection, CycleError message/sequence, topological ordering, critical path selection); no new pragma/pretense annotation was used because the dead logic was genuinely eliminated; static checks pass.
